<EditorialPageLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How SmartAbodeLab handles affiliate links, commercial relationships, product samples, advertising, and editorial independence."
  canonicalPath="/affiliate-disclosure"
  updated="August 8, 2026"
>
  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>Some SmartAbodeLab pages may contain affiliate links. If a reader follows an eligible link and makes a purchase, SmartAbodeLab may receive a commission without changing the price paid by the reader.</p>

  <h2>Editorial decisions remain independent</h2>
  <p>An affiliate relationship should not determine which products we cover, what we recommend, or how we describe strengths and weaknesses. A product should not receive a better conclusion because it offers a higher commission.</p>

  <h2>Disclosure on individual articles</h2>
  <p>When an article contains affiliate links or has another commercial relationship that could matter to a reader, the page should show a disclosure near the editorial content rather than hiding it only in this policy.</p>

  <h2>Review samples and early access</h2>
  <p>Manufacturers may provide review units or temporary access. When that happens and the relationship is material to evaluating the review, it should be disclosed. A supplied product does not guarantee publication or a positive recommendation.</p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>Advertising inventory is visually and technically separated from editorial content. Ads do not constitute editorial endorsements, and advertisers should not receive advance control over independent editorial conclusions.</p>

  <h2>Retailer choice</h2>
  <p>Where useful, articles may link to more than one seller or to a manufacturer's own information so readers can compare availability, price, warranty, or regional compatibility.</p>
</EditorialPageLayout>
